  "entries": {
    "096d66d1-41a5-5907-8567-9bb37b5579b3": {
      "text": "Name: CSV Duplicate Row Removal\nDescription: Reads a CSV file, removes exact duplicate rows based on all columns, and writes the deduplicated data to a new file while preserving the original.\nObjective: data cleaning\nAsset Type: session_skill\nGranularity: session\nAsset Node: workflow_skill\nAsset Path: family_root/macro_skill/workflow_skill\nAsset Level: 2\nDomain: data_processing\nDomain Type: default\nTaxonomy ID: default\nProfile ID: default::未分类技能\nFamily: 未分类技能\nTask Family: file_transformation\nMethod Family: deduplication\nStage: preprocessing\nApplicable Signals: input file path provided | output file path specified | no fuzzy matching criteria requested\nContraindications: data requires fuzzy or partial-row deduplication | row order must be preserved for time-series analysis | memory-constrained environment where full load is unsafe\nIntervention Moves: read_csv | drop_duplicates | to_csv\nWorkflow Steps: Validate input CSV file existence and readability. | Load CSV into tabular structure (e.g., pandas DataFrame). | Apply exact row-wise deduplication (keep='first'). | Validate output file path is writable and does not overwrite input. | Write deduplicated data to new CSV file with identical dialect and encoding. | Confirm original file checksum or mtime remains unchanged.\nConstraints: Input and output files must be on accessible local or mounted filesystem. | All columns participate in duplicate detection — no column subset override supported.\nCautions: Large files may exceed memory limits; warn before loading if size > 500MB. | Empty or malformed CSV may raise parsing errors — validate structure first.\nOutput Contract: A new CSV file containing only unique rows, with identical column structure, encoding, and dialect as input; original file byte-identical and unmodified.\nTriggers: user needs to clean CSV data | input has suspected duplicate rows | original file must remain unmodified\nTags: csv | deduplication | data cleaning | file transformation",
      "text_hash": "f39cd3816cbd154b4671bed82224ffd9ba10ee7235869d7fcc710273408f96fb",
